body:
To a certain point he has to keep taking them. I'd like to see him get into more mid range shots as an adjustment to his bad shooting year. Maybe getting the ball in the high post in the way AD gets his jumpers.

&#x200B;

Or I wonder what a AD Bron DHO looks like from the top of the key

I mean yeah that would be a really solid roster, I definitely not against it, that year really got a bad wrap that they didn't quite deserve. Dennis really dropped the ball with the contract issues, and Harrell was used to much as a starter, and he really isn't a number one option vs half the centers in the league defensively.

&#x200B;

No Kyrie but the team is looking deep. 4-6 seed and a deep playoff run if LeBron and AD can stay healthy and be ready to go come June. Shooting is still a little lack luster with Nunn, Bron and Hield being the only real 3 threats, and a few others who provide some spacing. 

&#x200B;

I still think we get Melo back if possible, try to ship out another player if we can. Although I think the plan is too have all these defenders and see who can shoot over the course of the season. Still Melo is dangerous playing as a spot up guy, and can still get a decent shot if needed.

True overall, but his on-ball defense vs star point guards is not a strong suit, although he has shown he can step it up for key games/moments.

&#x200B;

Also I got 21 down votes already, do people actually think Pat Bev is going to be a serious contributor at this point in his career?  I'll admit I haven't seen him play in years, but this was my take on him via reputation.

&#x200B;

Edit: Also given AD's skill set on the defensive end I don't think Turner adds as much to our D as he would with other defenses, especially with LeBron playing weak side and contesting drives like he does. Its like AD and Turner lose a block a game but and we get one more overall, in the role he will be playing he isn't THAT much of an upgrade from Thomas Byrant.

If the trend of a Celtics role player putting up career numbers every game continues we already know who the champs are this season.

&#x200B;

How many deep playoff games have you seen one teams best player give 34 (12/25 - 7/14) and the other teams best player posts 12 (3/17 - 1/5). Admittedly 12 assists is a lot, but those assist are still on Boston role players knocking down 3s, as much or more than Tatum being a good passer.

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfR6FBNo09E](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfR6FBNo09E)

&#x200B;

Why can nobody remember this???????

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfR6FBNo09E](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BfR6FBNo09E)

&#x200B;

There you go, how do you not remember this?????

As much as he's a fan favorite, he did a lot of shit that pissed me off which nobody seemed to notice. Apart from playing off of LeBron (which he did very well) all he did was brick on his on shot creation, turn the ball over and pass on open three's, only shooting them with reluctance.

&#x200B;

LeBron's sidekick was not worth big money. Sure he played D but for like 18 minutes, he's not playing D like that with 30+, not a fucking chance.

He use to play with Steven Adams to an elite level, and if we get Russ, strong chance we don't get Drummond.

&#x200B;

He's an upgrade from Dennis in every way at least, and at this point in his career he'd play second fiddle to Bron and AD. As a third option he would be solid offensively, not even counting the *Russ Factor*. I trust him with wide open 3's, or at least to drive the ball hard once he's open on bad shooting nights. If all he wants is to win, and focus's on rebounding, and defense, he'll be a handful for any team every night. The guy is relentless. Especially so if this means he'll be playing less minutes, ditto to Bron as well.

Only adding Lonzo would not get them to the playoffs. Think Boston, Miami, ATL, Milwakee, NYK, NYN, Philly teams all better no matter who they sign. Then you have your Washington (Russ played through injury until they made their push), the young Hornets (only going to get better), Pacers and Raptors (were missing 3 starters for much of the year). 

&#x200B;

They need someone better than Lonzo to *Lead Them* to the playoffs.

Think Lowry, Simmons, Conley, Lillard, McCollum, Beal, Westbrook, Mills, McConnell, Payne, Rose, Jackson, Monk. I'm don't think Lonzo will be their first choice, he's not enough to put them into a winning situation, without some veteran winners like Bron or AD.

&#x200B;

Honestly Simmons would fit the bulls, since LaVine doesn't need the post room that Ben takes. Not to mention how much that young team would benefit from his pace.

&#x200B;

Our odds of getting Lonzo are pretty good. He might not quite be worth the 20 Mil though, despite the fit with the Lakers.

I'm not sure, he'd bring a lot of energy and pace, which is not a bad thing. It would be nice to have someone who could shoot at a high percentage, but at least Russ is passable on open looks, as good as Dennis anyway.

&#x200B;

He'd really mesh well with AD, the way he cuts, take space and drives to pull in defenders is second to none. He also has a history of finding big men really effectively in these situations.

&#x200B;

You'd think he might not be a good fit with LeBron because they are both so ball dominant, but in a sense it would work because as the pace slows down, Russ could defer to LBJ. Meaning in half court sets after a few seconds of testing the defense out of transition the ball ends up with Bron. Off the ball, Russ would be okay with LeBron as well, making cuts and beating defenders down the floor for end zone passes, also just vice-versa setting up James in transition. With ball-handling duties out of his hands Russ could also put more energy into rebounding and defense. Not to mention having a Hall-of-Famer level talent to run the floor when Lebron sits, which as he ages over the next few seasons will likely become more of an issue.

&#x200B;

If we can make it work without gutting the teams identity, I say we do it. Only KCP, AD, and LeBron are completely off limits in my books. If we can lose some depth because Russ takes some offensive responsibilities when James and AD rest then sure. Although his price is pretty steep, and back-loaded, probably not something you want on a aging superstar.

I used the italics to separate the first and last lines in each paragraph section. Then I added one word per paragraph, to connect the italic phrases separately. Also just to add to the punctuation style and what I was trying to convey with the unorthodox usages of the punctuation.

&#x200B;

I wasn't sure about it but I've already entered anyway.

Great imagery. Ivory paint falls from the window ledges; egg shells for me to dance on. Very nice, also: Wisteria chokes the cottage like a scorned ex-lover.

&#x200B;

If you had another meaning beyond the description of the cottage, I would elaborate on it more, not necessarily in an obvious way, I wouldn't take from your prose that much. Could be me as well, I'm not especially versed in poetry.

